The Most Plausible God

My video-making process is not very efficient. I don't start making a video until an idea gets stuck in my head and the only way to stop it from plaguing my mind is to make a video about it. Psychologically, that sort of gives me permission to move on. There's no big plan. I don't base my videos on what I think is trending or what I think will make the most money. I base them on the sorts of things incessantly occupying my mind at that time. My hope is that people listen because they're interested in what I personally have to say about it.

That being said, I never planned to make a video about this, but it fits my criterion, because I keep thinking about it. So, I have to get it off my chest.

I've made video after video arguing against a god that half the world believes in, the Abrahamic god of the Christians, Muslims, and Jews. I've done so because half the world believes in it, despite it being one of the most unlikely gods. What I have never talked about, however, is which god would be the MOST likely. There has to be one, right? Well, there is one, and frankly, I have no arguments against it. That doesn't mean I believe in it, because I still don't have specific enough evidence to be conclusive, but I see no logical issues with it either. So, in my next video I'll explore it a bit and see what you think.

Beyond that video, I was thinking about maybe doing a political video before the midterms. Of course, I'm always thinking about politics, but it would be impractical for me to do so many videos on an ever-changing subject. So, I just deal with never getting a lot of that off my chest. The midterms could be an important inflection point, however, so it might be worthwhile at this time. What do you think? Would it even matter at this point?    and posted reply : IMO there is only one 'god' iow overwhelming thing in the universe that affects all and his name is "Murphy" aka 'RNG' aka 'Chaos' aka 'Sheet happens' I got one thumbs up (:

